  "seoBody": "<div class=\"key-takeaways\"><strong>Key takeaways</strong><ul><li>Care home audit software covers three common walks: mock CQC quality audits, health and safety environment checks, and infection prevention and control audits</li><li>CQC regulates in England; the Care Inspectorate covers Scotland, Care Inspectorate Wales covers Wales, and RQIA covers Northern Ireland, so the framework varies by nation</li><li>Most staff never fill in a dedicated app on the floor; they complete it later from memory, and the evidence suffers</li><li>Charging 20 pounds per active user a month, dormant users free, beats per-seat for a care group, because you only pay for who works</li><li>Quickler audits the environment, premises and process; it complements a care management system, does not replace one, and is not a clinical record</li></ul></div><h2>What care home audit software is actually for</h2><p>A care provider generates a steady stream of internal audits: mock inspections against the regulator's framework, health and safety walks, infection control checks, environment and premises audits, mealtime and dignity observations. Each has its own checklist and its own audience, from the registered manager to a regional quality team to the regulator at inspection. What they share is that the record has to be accurate, timestamped and backed by evidence, and it has to survive scrutiny.</p><p>Software does not make a home compliant. The registered manager acting on the findings does. What software does is make the audit easier to complete correctly on the floor, harder to skip an item, and faster to turn into a report and an action plan. A good tool means nobody back-fills a mock inspection from memory in the office at the end of the week.</p><h2>The three common care home audits</h2><h3>1. Mock CQC quality audit</h3><p>A mock inspection walks the home against the regulator's framework before the real one arrives. In England that is CQC's single assessment framework and its five key questions: safe, effective, caring, responsive and well-led, broken down into quality statements. The audit gathers the evidence a manager would want to show an inspector, and flags the gaps early. See the CQC compliance audit checklist for the detail.</p><h3>2. Health and safety environment audit</h3><p>The care environment carries duties under the Health and Safety at Work etc Act 1974: falls, moving and handling, hoists and slings under LOLER, legionella management, and fire under the Regulatory Reform (Fire Safety) Order 2005. The audit walks each area and records the state of each control.</p><h3>3. Infection prevention and control audit</h3><p>IPC audits check the environment against the code of practice on the prevention and control of infections: hand hygiene stations, PPE stock and use, cleaning standards, and the general state of the premises. The record ties each finding to a location and a photo.</p><h2>The regulator varies by nation</h2><p>In England the Care Quality Commission regulates adult social care under the Health and Social Care Act 2008 (Regulated Activities) Regulations 2014 and the fundamental standards. The rest of the UK differs: the Care Inspectorate in Scotland, Care Inspectorate Wales in Wales, and RQIA in Northern Ireland, each with its own quality framework. Quickler lets a firm build the audit around whichever framework applies rather than hard-coding one nation's checklist. Check the current guidance for your regulator, and treat this as general information, not legal advice.</p><h2>What to look for in care home audit software</h2><ul><li><strong>On-the-floor completion:</strong> the tool should make it easier to complete the audit during the walk, not afterwards</li><li><strong>Photo evidence at the point of observation:</strong> each finding tied to a timestamped image and a location, not a folder sorted out that evening</li><li><strong>A live dashboard across homes:</strong> the group should see every home's audit status without chasing managers for spreadsheets</li><li><strong>No per-seat penalty:</strong> per-seat pricing punishes a group for its bank staff and office team. Quickler charges 20 pounds per active user a month, dormant users free, so you only pay for who works</li><li><strong>Clear scope:</strong> the tool audits the environment and process; it does not replace the care record</li></ul><div class=\"callout\"><strong>Honest note:</strong> Quickler captures the audit and evidence and gives the group a live dashboard. It does not make the home compliant, and it is not a care management system or a clinical record. The registered manager acting on the findings carries the compliance. <a href=\"/pages/help/index.html#contact-form-section\">Ask us</a> if that distinction matters for your firm.</div><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>What is care home audit software?</h3><p>It is any tool that helps a manager or auditor record an internal audit and produce a report: mock CQC inspections, health and safety walks, infection control checks, environment and premises audits. Options range from paper folders, to generic audit apps like iAuditor, to conversation-based tools like quickler that run the workflow over WhatsApp so there is no app to install and the group sees every home on one dashboard.</p><h3>Does Quickler replace our care management system?</h3><p>No. Quickler audits the environment, premises and process. It complements a care management system, it does not replace one, and it is not a clinical record. It does not hold care plans or medication records. Keep those in your care planning system and use quickler for the compliance and environment audit trail around them.</p><h3>Does it work outside England, where CQC does not regulate?</h3><p>Yes. CQC regulates in England, but the Care Inspectorate covers Scotland, Care Inspectorate Wales covers Wales and RQIA covers Northern Ireland, each with its own framework. Quickler lets the firm build the audit around whichever framework applies rather than hard-coding one nation's checklist. Check the current guidance for your regulator.</p><h3>Can I run care audits over WhatsApp?</h3><p>Yes. Quickler's workflows run over the WhatsApp Business API. The auditor receives each question in their existing WhatsApp chat, replies with text, a voice note or a photo, and the completed report generates automatically. No separate app or login is required, and quickler manages the WhatsApp Business API account on the firm's behalf.</p><h3>Related guides</h3><ul><li><a href=\"/pages/cqc-compliance-audit-checklist-uk.html\">CQC compliance audit checklist</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/care-home-health-safety-audit-uk.html\">Care home health and safety audit</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/ipc-audit-care-home-uk.html\">IPC audit for care homes</a></li></ul>",
